+## Turn usage (issue #93)
+
+The hook keeps one optional usage argument containing the summed turn usage. A separate per-round breakdown is rejected for this change because the consumer need is turn billing and budgeting; provider-call detail would widen the API without being needed for that use case. The public signature must name this as total turn usage, and the release must include a MINOR bump and a changelog entry explaining the larger numbers for existing consumers of tool-heavy turns.
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the sum of input, output and total tokens across every provider call, including both tool rounds and the final answer. ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call after two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/usage.acceptance.test.ts#L60))
+- Missing usage on any round is ignored when summing reported rounds; if no round reports usage, the hook still receives `undefined`, and a no-tool turn preserves its provider's usage unchanged. ([validated by: counts reported rounds when usage is missing and preserves an entirely unreported turn](../../src/orchestration/usage.acceptance.test.ts#L70))
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The non-Error rejection behaviour remains outside issue #93.
 
-- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
